The pews.~
   This rickety, wooden structure creeks and shudders with every step.  The
dirty rug beneath stretches all the way to the altar and bears the wear and
tear of over a century of use.  Flanking you are several cramped rows of pews
with barely enough room to kneel between them.  Once ornately carved and
decorated, this pride of some ancient carpenter has deteriorated greatly
throughout the years.  Shallow imprints from the many people who sat in them
mar the pews' surfaces, and the once detailed carvings are chipped and worn
down to an almost unrecognizable state.  Behind you is the entrance to this
building.  Stained glass windows adorn the buildings surroundings.  Depicting
something.  In front lies the altar.  From here the picture can just be made
out.  It is a man is nailed to the cross.  He is almost nude and hangs limply.
The altar gleams slightly.    
~
